# Environment variable convention (#40)
#
# This file exists to establish the convention ahead of the epics that need
# one:
#   - Epic #3 (Anthropic / AI SDK key for Claude Haiku 4.5)
#   - Epic #5 (Upstash rate limiting) — #39 below is the first variable set.
#   - Epic #6 (Neon Postgres / pgvector)
#
# The MCP endpoint mounted at apps/web/app/api/mcp/route.ts (#11) itself needs
# none: mcp-handler 2.x (the current major, verified against its published
# docs while building #11) removed the redisUrl/basePath/sessionIdGenerator
# config options entirely — the endpoint is stateless and mounted directly at
# its route, with no external service or base-URL configuration to inject.
# Rate limiting IN FRONT of that endpoint (#39, below) is a separate concern.
#
# Real values are never committed. They live in:
#   - Local development: an untracked `.env.local` in `apps/web/` (git-ignored, see .gitignore).
#   - Preview and Production: Vercel project settings (Project -> Settings -> Environment
#     Variables), scoped per environment (Development / Preview / Production).
#
# When a new variable is introduced, add a commented placeholder line for it here
# (NAME=), e.g.:
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
#
# SITE_URL — optional override for the site's own absolute origin, read by
# apps/web/src/lib/config/site-url.ts (#43). Not required: on Vercel the
# origin is derived automatically from the VERCEL_URL/VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL
# system env vars Vercel injects for every deploy, and falls back to
# http://localhost:3000 locally. Set this only to pin the origin to something
# else (e.g. a future custom domain) ahead of DNS actually pointing at it.
# SITE_URL=

# Rate limiting for /api/mcp (#39) — see apps/web/README.md "Rate limiting"
# for the full writeup (canonical documentation; link here rather than
# duplicate). Backed by Upstash Redis (free tier) via @upstash/ratelimit.
#
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL / UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN — REST credentials for the
# Upstash Redis database (created in the Upstash console, REST API tab).
# Required for rate limiting to actually run. If either is unset — local dev
# without them, CI (which is never given these credentials on purpose), or a
# forked PR's preview deploy — the endpoint FAILS OPEN: it serves MCP traffic
# with no limiting instead of erroring, and logs a loud console.warn. Never
# commit real values; set them in Vercel project settings (Production +
# Preview) instead.
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=

# RATELIMIT_MAX_REQUESTS / RATELIMIT_WINDOW_SECONDS — override the sliding-
# window quota (default: 60 requests per 60-second window per caller IP —
# generous for an interactive AI assistant driving a handful of tool calls
# per turn). Any unset, non-numeric, non-integer, or non-positive value falls
# back to its default rather than erroring.
# RATELIMIT_MAX_REQUESTS=60
# RATELIMIT_WINDOW_SECONDS=60

# Embedded Mastra interview agent chat model provider (#63) — see
# packages/agent/README.md for the full writeup (canonical documentation;
# link here rather than duplicate), including why the default was inverted
# from the original issue text (Gemini free tier default, Anthropic as the
# swappable alternate).
#
# CHAT_PROVIDER — "google" (default) or "anthropic". Selects which AI SDK
# provider binding packages/agent's createChatModel() resolves.
# CHAT_PROVIDER=google

# CHAT_MODEL_ID — optional override of the selected provider's default
# model id (google: gemini-3.5-flash-lite, anthropic: claude-haiku-4-5).
#
# Quota rationale (verified against the AI Studio dashboard; corroborated by
# #141's recorded `429 RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED` — quotaId
# GenerateRequestsPerDayPerProjectPerModel-FreeTier, quotaValue 20 — for the
# former default, gemini-3.6-flash) for why the pinned lite id is the
# default rather than a full flash model or the `-latest` alias:
#
#   Model                    | Free tier RPM | Free tier RPD
#   ------------------------ | -------------- | --------------
#   gemini-3.6-flash         | 5              | 20
#   gemini-3.7-flash         | 5              | 20
#   gemini-3.5-flash-lite    | 15             | 500   <- default (pinned id)
#   gemini-3.1-flash-lite    | 15             | 500
#
# 20 requests/day is tight enough that a single eval run can exhaust it
# before counting production chat traffic on the same key; the lite tier's
# 500/day gives both room to share the free tier. Pinned (not `-latest`) so
# a silent upstream model swap can't change eval/production behavior
# out from under this project.
# CHAT_MODEL_ID=

# GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY — required when CHAT_PROVIDER=google (or
# unset, since google is the default). Get a free-tier key from Google AI
# Studio. Missing this when google is selected fails fast with a descriptive
# error naming the variable — never its value.
#
# Also required by the ingestion pipeline (#24, epic #6, `pnpm ingest` — see
# docs/development.md "Ingestion pipeline") regardless of CHAT_PROVIDER: the
# same Google account's key embeds career-data chunks with
# `gemini-embedding-001` (truncated to 768 dimensions — model id and
# dimension live in packages/core/src/embedding/config.ts, the single place
# ingestion and the future searchCareer (#34) both read them from). Missing
# this when running `pnpm ingest` fails fast the same way, naming the
# variable, never its value.
# GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY=

# EMBED_MAX_TEXTS_PER_MINUTE — optional, defaults to 80 (#317, epic #6).
# Caps how many texts `pnpm ingest`/`pnpm eval:retrieval` embed in any
# trailing 60 seconds, so a full ingest (~190 texts) never trips Gemini's
# free-tier per-minute limit (100, counted in texts, not calls). No "off"
# value — pacing is always applied. A value below the embedder's batch
# size (16) doesn't error, it just shrinks the effective batch size to
# match. See docs/development.md "Ingestion pipeline" for the daily-budget
# math.
# EMBED_MAX_TEXTS_PER_MINUTE=80

# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY — required only when CHAT_PROVIDER=anthropic. Not set in
# this project's Vercel environments by default; the Anthropic binding is
# still fully constructible and tested with a fake key injected in tests.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Chat guardrails for /api/chat (#68) — see apps/web/README.md "Chat
# guardrails" for the full writeup (canonical documentation; link here
# rather than duplicate). Rate limiting reuses the same Upstash Redis
# credentials as #39 above, under distinct key namespaces.
#
# CHAT_SESSION_RATELIMIT_MAX_REQUESTS / CHAT_SESSION_RATELIMIT_WINDOW_SECONDS
# — override the per-session sliding-window quota (default: 20 requests per
# 5-minute window). Same malformed-value-falls-back-to-default behavior as
# RATELIMIT_MAX_REQUESTS above.
# CHAT_SESSION_RATELIMIT_MAX_REQUESTS=20
# CHAT_SESSION_RATELIMIT_WINDOW_SECONDS=300

# CHAT_IP_RATELIMIT_MAX_REQUESTS / CHAT_IP_RATELIMIT_WINDOW_SECONDS — override
# the per-IP backstop quota (default: 40 requests per 5-minute window),
# checked independently of sessionId so rotating it doesn't evade the limit.
# CHAT_IP_RATELIMIT_MAX_REQUESTS=40
# CHAT_IP_RATELIMIT_WINDOW_SECONDS=300

# CHAT_AGENT_MAX_STEPS — override the per-turn agent step/tool-call cap
# (default: 8). Any unset, non-numeric, non-integer, or non-positive value
# falls back to the default.
# CHAT_AGENT_MAX_STEPS=8

# Neon Postgres + pgvector store (#14, epic #6) — see
# packages/core/README.md "Database (Neon pgvector store)" for the full
# writeup (canonical documentation; link here rather than duplicate),
# including the embedding-dimension/distance-metric ADR and how to run the
# migration CLI and the real-Neon integration suite locally.
#
# DATABASE_URL — Postgres connection string for the `@hire-me-mcp/core/db`
# module (migrations, ingestion, searchCareer). Neon's pooled connection
# string (Dashboard -> Connect -> "Pooled connection") works as-is. Required
# for `pnpm --filter @hire-me-mcp/core db:migrate`; unit tests never need it
# (they're network-free) and the integration suite skips cleanly, with a
# console message, when it's absent.
# DATABASE_URL=

# NEON_API_KEY / NEON_PROJECT_ID — personal API key and project id used only
# to create and delete a throwaway Neon branch for the DB integration test
# suite (src/db/rag-store.integration.test.ts) — never used to touch the
# main database directly. Both must be set together for that suite to run;
# either missing (the default for local dev and most CI jobs) makes it skip
# with a clear message rather than failing or silently passing.
# NEON_API_KEY=
# NEON_PROJECT_ID=

# Anonymized usage analytics (#79, epic #8) — see docs/analytics.md for the
# event schema, taxonomy, and retention window.
#
# CRON_SECRET — the bearer token Vercel signs its own cron invocations with
# (https://vercel.com/docs/cron-jobs/manage-cron-jobs#securing-cron-jobs),
# checked by app/api/cron/analytics-retention/route.ts against the request's
# Authorization header. Required in Vercel Project Settings for Preview and
# Production; left unset in local dev, the route treats every request as
# authorized rather than locking itself out.
# CRON_SECRET=
#
# STATS_SECRET (#81) — the token gating the private stats view at
# GET /api/stats?token=$STATS_SECRET (app/api/stats/handler.ts). Unlike
# CRON_SECRET, this route is meant to be opened directly in a browser, so
# the token travels as a query param, not an Authorization header — and
# unlike CRON_SECRET's "unset means authorized" stance, this route is
# fail-closed: a missing secret, a wrong token, and a nonexistent route all
# return the same 404 (never 401), so nothing about the route leaks.
# Required in Vercel Project Settings for Preview and Production; left
# unset in local dev, the route always 404s. Generate a real value with
# `openssl rand -hex 32` — never commit the actual value.
# STATS_SECRET=
